  "summary": "V5 fixes the source-scale and mip-boundary defects found in V4: its sixteen project-owned frames are distinct at a 32 px-per-cell review mip, retain black cell boundaries, and represent individual ribbons, droplets, porous mist kernels, and foam crescents rather than complete macro plumes. Native review assets compile, load, and validate in an isolated package. The uncalibrated candidate is effectively invisible at gameplay distance. A V5-only optical-density calibration removes the production atlas's broad smoke puff in the close particle-macro comparison and reveals an irregular, hole-bearing water-film silhouette without rectangular edges, but that silhouette still collapses into a small detached fuzzy mark in the established contact camera and produces no material wrap-view improvement. Expanding only the mist mip footprint does not solve that gameplay-scale read. V5 therefore fails the visual-improvement gate. Production remains selected and byte-identical.",
